@* A section RCL does NOT inherit the host's Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Omitting a line
   here ships broken markup with a green build and no runtime error — see design §1/§2.

   Two localizers by design (design §15 step 3b, Governance's two-marker variant): the
   section owns its 12 Search_Filter* / Search_Global* keys, and SharedResource keeps
   Search_MinChars, which Shell's /Profile/Search page renders too — carving one key out of
   that page's four-key message set to claim it would split the set.

   The Humans bucket renders one <vc:user-search-result> per row — Users' own component,
   keyed by user id (nobodies-collective/Humans#1062). The orchestrator passes ids and match
   context and names no Users display field, but the element only binds because of the
   @addTagHelper below: drop that line and every row ships as inert literal markup on a green
   200. Guarded by SearchPageRenderTests (step 12). *@
@using Humans.Search
@using Humans.Search.Models
@using Humans.Search.Services.Dtos
@using Humans.Base
@using Humans.Base.Extensions
@using Humans.Users.Contracts
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.ViewFeatures
@* Index.cshtml @injects IConfiguration for the Features:Events flag; Sdk.Razor's implicit
   usings are a subset of Sdk.Web's and do not carry it. *@
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Localization
@inject IStringLocalizer<SearchResource> Localizer
@inject IStringLocalizer<SharedResource> SharedLocalizer
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@addTagHelper *, Humans.Base
@* <vc:user-search-result> is the Users section's own component. *@
@addTagHelper *, Humans.Users
